# Implementation Plan — Small Phases

## Overview
Break the full roadmap into 6 small, independently-shippable phases. Each phase is scoped to a few files and can be built+tested before moving on.

---

## Phase 1A: Security Hardening & Code Quality (First)

Adds global exception handling, rate limiting, and fixes code quality issues that affect all users.

### [NEW] Middleware/GlobalExceptionMiddleware.cs
- Catches all unhandled exceptions
- Returns standardized JSON error responses (`{ error, statusCode, traceId }`)
- Logs full exception details server-side, returns safe messages to clients
- Registered in `Program.cs`

### [MODIFY] [Program.cs](file:///c:/Users/samar/source/repos/FinancialApplication/FinancialApplication.Api/Program.cs)
- Add `Microsoft.AspNetCore.RateLimiting` with fixed-window limiter (100 req/min general, 10 req/min for auth endpoints)
- Make CORS origins configurable via `appsettings.json` instead of hardcoded `localhost:5173`
- Replace `Console.WriteLine` in JWT events with `ILogger`
- Register the global exception middleware

### [MODIFY] [appsettings.json](file:///c:/Users/samar/source/repos/FinancialApplication/FinancialApplication.Api/appsettings.json)
- Add `AllowedOrigins` array for CORS
- Add `RateLimiting` section

### Code Quality Fixes (in same phase):
- Rename `_Logout` → `LogoutAsync` in [IAuthService.cs](file:///c:/Users/samar/source/repos/FinancialApplication/FinancialApplication.Application/Interfaces/IAuthService.cs) and its implementation
- Fix `RefereshToken` → `RefreshToken` typo across file names and class references
- Rename `Transaction.cs.cs` → `Transaction.cs`

